From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nelson Gill <ngill@slack-corp.com>
Date: Wed, 13 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: fix: use org.kde SNI bus name prefix for snap confinement

Chromium 151+ changed the StatusNotifierItem well-known bus name from
org.kde.StatusNotifierItem-{PID} to
org.freedesktop.StatusNotifierItem-{PID}-{service_id}.

Under snap strict confinement, the unity7 interface only grants:
  dbus (bind) bus=session name=org.kde.StatusNotifierItem-[0-9]*

The org.freedesktop prefix is not covered by any snap interface, causing
AppArmor to deny the bus name registration and making the tray icon
invisible for all Electron snap apps.

The StatusNotifierItem specification and all known StatusNotifierWatcher
implementations accept either prefix -- the bus name is just an ownership
claim on the session bus and does not affect the SNI protocol. Restoring
the org.kde prefix matches what Chromium <151 used and is compatible with
all desktop environments.

Upstream snapd bug: https://bugs.launchpad.net/snapd/+bug/2161950

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/status_icons/status_icon_linux_dbus.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/status_icons/status_icon_linux_dbus.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/status_icons/status_icon_linux_dbus.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/status_icons/status_icon_linux_dbus.cc
@@ -298,7 +298,7 @@ void StatusIconLinuxDbus::OnHostRegisteredResponse(
   service_id_ = NextServiceId();

   service_name_ =
-      base::StrCat({"org.freedesktop.StatusNotifierItem-",
+      base::StrCat({"org.kde.StatusNotifierItem-",
                     base::NumberToString(base::Process::Current().Pid()), "-",
                     base::NumberToString(service_id_)});

